 "notes": [
  "Pual participle_passive Ruth.2.1 (מידע, ketiv, unvocalized, \"a kinsman\") was invisible before the pipeline's ketiv-extraction fix -- single attestation, low confidence. Its qere, מוֹדָע, is a distinct noun (H4129) with the same \"kinsman/acquaintance\" meaning, so this is a spelling/lexical-choice variant rather than a different sense, but the numbers differ so the ketiv is kept as its own attestation per the fix's rule. \"One known\" (a passive participle of \"know\") substantivized as \"acquaintance/kinsman\" is a well-attested Semitic pattern, distinct enough from the root's primary \"know\" sense to warrant its own stem_gloss."
